      Task 214 (H8-B rewrite, commit a26e30dd2, SESSION 21) removed the last C# code path referencing `spe-app-cert`. The new `SpeConfidentialClientGraphFactory` reads cert from `SPE-OwnerCert-Pfx` (per `SpeContainerOptions.DefaultCertSecretName`).

      During task 214.7 KV manifest work, grep verification surfaced remaining consumers in `config/spaarke-resources.yaml` (declarative dev-env manifest) + `scripts/Import-And-Register.ps1` (bootstrap script — likely non-functional since cert thumbprint drift discovered 2026-08-30). Deferred to this follow-on task rather than shipped inside 214 commit to keep 214's scope clean.

      KV cert drift discovered 2026-08-30 (task 213.2 Option A H8 live-test): KV `spaarke-spekvcert/spe-app-cert` thumbprint `269691A5A60536050FA76C0163BD4A942ECD724D` (CN=SPE Certificate 22Sept2025_1) is NOT registered on any Spaarke app-reg. SDAP-PCF-CLIENT `170c98e1-...` has a different cert registered (`A57B48A2...` CN=SDAP-SPE-Owner-Renewed-2026). So the KV secrets are dead weight — no app-reg would accept a JWT signed by them.

      Task 186 dispatch is NOT blocked by 215.
    </background>
