  <constraints>
    <constraint source="kv-credential-lifecycle-rule-4">E-1 secrets (per-customer SpeAdmin container-type secrets — includes `spe-owning-app-secret` per topology doc §3A row 1 owning-app rotation lifecycle) are OUT OF SCOPE and MUST stay protected indefinitely. Only retire `spe-app-cert` + `spe-app-cert-pass`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="kv-credential-lifecycle-rule-1">Never re-introduce `BFF-API-ClientSecret` (either casing) under any name. Not directly relevant here (different secret) but a reminder: task 215 must NOT create any replacement secret; it's pure retirement.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-35-precheck-gate">BEFORE the KV soft-delete (215.3), verify LIVE App Service settings + KV `referenced` list + any Dataverse-persisted config do NOT reference the retiring secrets. The declarative config check + grep sweep in 215.1 satisfies this for the code + docs surface; a `az webapp config appsettings list` sweep against `spaarke-bff-dev` App Service also recommended.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spaarke-resources-yaml-lifecycle-conventions">File's own convention (lines 11-19): retired resources MUST carry a `_meta:` block with `status: retired`, `retired: {date}`, `reason_retained: "..."`, `history: [...]`. 215.2 MUST honor this convention rather than deleting the entries silently.</constraint>
    <constraint source="soft-delete-not-purge">Use `az keyvault secret delete` (soft-delete, 90-day recovery) NOT `az keyvault secret purge` (irreversible). Purge is only appropriate for confirmed-orphan secrets after the recovery window expires.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>Grep verification `git grep -n "spe-app-cert" -- '*.cs' '*.ps1' '*.yaml' '*.yml' '*.json'` returns only expected files (config/spaarke-resources.yaml retirement notes + scripts/_archive/ or scripts/Import-And-Register.ps1 header + projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/** self-references + runs/h8-live-test-2026-08-30.md evidence).</criterion>
    <criterion>`config/spaarke-resources.yaml` cert_secrets block carries `_meta: status: retired` per file's own convention. `keyvault_inventory` splits `referenced` from `retired_but_present_in_kv` for the two soft-deleted secrets.</criterion>
    <criterion>`scripts/Import-And-Register.ps1` is either archived (Option A: moved to scripts/_archive/) OR carries a DEPRECATED banner + throw (Option C: parity with task 213.3 pattern). Rationale documented in task 215 notes.</criterion>
    <criterion>Azure KV `spaarke-spekvcert/spe-app-cert` + `spe-app-cert-pass` are soft-deleted (verify via `az keyvault secret list-deleted --vault-name spaarke-spekvcert`). Both appear in the deleted list. NOT purged.</criterion>
    <criterion>Azure KV `spaarke-spekvcert/spe-owning-app-secret` UNTOUCHED (verify via `az keyvault secret show --vault-name spaarke-spekvcert --name spe-owning-app-secret` returns 200).</criterion>
    <criterion>`spaarke-bff-dev` App Service settings sweep (`az webapp config appsettings list -g rg-spaarke-dev -n spaarke-bff-dev`) shows NO references to `spe-app-cert` or `spe-app-cert-pass`.</criterion>
    <criterion>Task 215 completion note captures: (1) grep sweep result before + after retirement; (2) which fate chosen for Import-And-Register.ps1 (A/B/C) + why; (3) KV soft-delete operator commands executed + evidence; (4) confirmation that spe-owning-app-secret preserved.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

